[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1657","stub":{"id":"1657","section":"T359 to Towanda Creek","altname":"","river":"Schrader Creek","difficulty":"IItoIV","states":["USA-PEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"261","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112252","location":{"latitude":"41.6255989074707","longitude":"-76.6564025878906"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117535","location":{"latitude":"41.7078018188477","longitude":"-76.506103515625"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"12.7","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"2589","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1622","description":"","caption":"Last Drop","poi_name":"Lamoka","subject":"Steve Graley (Phantomboater )","author":"Geren","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2589","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2589"}},{"id":"6045","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1621","description":"If the Towanda Creek gauge is 8' or higher, then this creek starts to liven up.","caption":"Three waves...Three Boaters....","poi_name":"3 Wave","subject":"Phil, Kevin, and Jay","author":"Phantomboater","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6045","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6045"}},{"id":"17087","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1623","description":"After a 150 yards of Class III- IV- rock dodge, you end up at the last drop that is deceiving, but with a nice recovery pool.....","caption":"Fantumboater @ Lamoka Drop","poi_name":"Lamoka....at the end","subject":"Stevie \"G\"","author":"Brent Burke","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/17087","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/17087"}},{"id":"6046","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1621","description":"This is a long rapid, with plenty to surprise you. Holes, diagonal ledges, trees, and lengthy run.  Swimming is not acceptible this time of year.","caption":"Open Boater ? This time of the year ?","poi_name":"1st Class IV Section","subject":"Chuckie O.","author":"Phantomboater","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6046","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6046"}},{"id":"6926","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7060","description":"Flipped not too far up from this final drop on the Lamoka section but got the combat roll up and ran the drop clean.  ","caption":"Final Drop","poi_name":"Lamoka","subject":"Geren","author":"Jamie?","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6926","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6926"}},{"id":"6047","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1621","description":"After finally getting my frozen skirt on, and dodging the rocks and holes, I come to the \"ledgey\" section, near the end, trying to avoid the last hole....barely.","caption":"1/2 way down","poi_name":"1st Class IV Section","subject":"Phantomboater","author":"Thomas O.","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6047","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6047"}},{"id":"6053","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1621","description":"Check out the full-sized version of this great photo by <a href=\"http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=6045\">clicking here</a>.","caption":"Three waves...Three Boaters....","poi_name":"3 Wave","subject":"Phil, Kevin, and Jay","author":"Phantomboater","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6053","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6053"}},{"id":"6927","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7059","description":"This recirculates and he got recirculated.  This is as far as his forward progress went and shows him in the process of falling over.  Stud manages something like 3 offside combat rolls and finally surfs it around into the outflowing water, back towards the center of the creek.  Flips again in the squirrels but rolls once again.  Wish I got more pictures of that action.  ","caption":"Yeeha","poi_name":"Lamoka","subject":"Jamie","author":"Geren","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6927","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6927"}}],"detail":{"id":"1657","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Jeff Mitchell sez:\n\n\"Schrader Creek is a beautiful stream located in a wilderness setting with very little development. Most of the creek is within state game lands. It is about 20-30 feet wide, a little smaller than the [Loyalsock](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1632/), but just as beautiful. Strainers are few and what strainers do exist have been pushed up on the bank. Most rapids formed by boulders; some are quite large. The creek has many rapids, some continuous. Below Falls Creek, there is a long boulder garden. A few miles downstream the creek's channel narrows as it flows over a series of ledges. Average gradient is about 50 f/p/m.\"\n\nLat/longitude coords are approximate, from TopoZone.","averageGradient":"50","maxGradient":null,"length":"12.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1657","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":n